      "content": "Traditionalist theologians typically argue that modern redefinings of marriage and family undermine the \"natural law\" principle that a union must be one, exclusive, and procreative. They contend that unessentialist definitions erode the moral foundation of the family unit, reducing it to a mere legal contract rather than a covenants sanctified by divine or natural order. Consequently, they assert that these shifts do not just alter social consensus but actively conflict with a transcendent truth that cannot be morally compromised by political or cultural opinion.",
